 "notes": "The list has 26 stations, lines 245-277, under three printed sub-headings: \"East Coast of Scotland.\" (line 242), \"Orkney.\" (251) and \"Mainland.\" (261). No type (L.H./L.V.) is printed for any row. The lead-in quote was repeated in the prompt, but the only key to the marks is \"(_a_) Describes a bird but no schedule.\" (line 279).\n\nHow I filled the fields:\n- Asterisks: each asterisk sits under one year of the header \"1879, '80, '81, '82.\" (line 244), at text columns 4, 10, 15 and 20. In `marks` I kept their spacing as printed, so you can tell the years apart.\n  - All four years (1879-'82): Sumburgh Head, North Ronaldshay, Auskerry, Pentland Skerries, Bell Rock, Isle of May.\n  - '80, '81, '82: Whalsey Skerries, Dunnet Head, Inch Keith.\n  - 1879 and '80: North Uist.\n  - '81 and '82: Cromarty.\n  - '82 only: Bressay, Chanonry Point.\n- Kinnaird Head: it has no asterisks, only \"(_a_)\" printed in the year area under '81/'82. Which year it refers to isn't clear.\n- Heights: \"230 ft.\" on the first row; every later row has a number followed by a ditto mark (\") meaning \"ft.\" I put these in `other` exactly as printed, spacing included.\n- Fair Isle (7B): the height is printed as \"?\". No place is printed for it, though it is under the Shetland group.\n- Montroseness: the second quoted item, \"No birds.\", is a remark, not a keeper. It is in `other` after the height.\n- Keepers: I left off the full stop that ends each row (printed \"J. Wilson.\" → \"J. Wilson\"). The full stop is in the fragments.\n- Fragments: each is the whole printed line, including leading spaces.\n\nCopied as printed but probably wrong:\n- \"North Uist, Shetland\" is almost certainly a misprint for North Unst (Muckle Flugga); North Uist is in the Outer Hebrides.\n- \"Whalsey Skerries\" is probably the Out Skerries lighthouse (Bound Skerry) off Whalsay. The spelling is as printed.\n- \"Chanonry Point, Elgin\": Chanonry is in Ross-shire (Black Isle), not Elgin.\n- \"Montroseness, Aberdeen\": Montrose (Scurdie Ness) is in Forfarshire, not Aberdeen.\n- \"Cromarty, East Cromarty\", \"Tarbat Ness, East Ross\" and \"Bell Rock, Fife Coast\" are printed localities, copied as given.\n- \"D. M Scott.\" is missing a full stop or apostrophe (probably \"D. M. Scott\" or \"D. M'Scott\").\n- \"Inch Keith\" is printed as two words.\n- \"D. MacDonald\" (Pentland Skerries) and \"J. Macdonald\" (Auskerry) are spelled differently.\n- Rows 8-14 have one space between the ditto mark and the keeper. Rows 5 and 7 have two.",
